-- title:
--   Eqs. (2.6)–(2.7) — per-step descent inequality of Algorithm 1 and its summed form
-- statement:
--   Let $H$ be a real Hilbert space, $A, B$ maximal monotone, $C$ $\beta$-cocoercive with $\beta > 0$, $J_A = J_{\gamma A}$, $J_B = J_{\gamma B}$ the resolvents, and $T$ the operator of Eq. (1.2). Let $\varepsilon \in (0,1)$, $\gamma \in (0, 2\beta\varepsilon)$, $\alpha = 1/(2-\varepsilon)$, $(\lambda_j)_{j\ge0} \subseteq (0, 1/\alpha)$, $\tau_k = \lambda_k(1-\lambda_k) + \lambda_k(1-\alpha)/\alpha$, and let $(z^k)$, $(x_B^k)$ be generated by Algorithm 1 from $z^0 \in H$. Let $z^* \in \operatorname{Fix} T$. Then for every $k \ge 0$
--   $$\|z^{k+1} - z^*\|^2 + \tau_k\|Tz^k - z^k\|^2 + \gamma\lambda_k\Big(2\beta - \frac{\gamma}{\varepsilon}\Big)\|Cx_B^k - CJ_{\gamma B}(z^*)\|^2 \le \|z^k - z^*\|^2. \tag{2.6}$$
--   Moreover, if $\underline{\lambda} > 0$ satisfies $\underline{\lambda} \le \lambda_j$ for all $j$, then for every $k \ge 0$ the series below converges and
--   $$\sum_{i=k}^\infty \|Cx_B^i - CJ_{\gamma B}(z^*)\|^2 \le \frac{\|z^k - z^*\|^2}{\gamma\,\underline{\lambda}\,\big(2\beta - \gamma/\varepsilon\big)}. \tag{2.7}$$
--
--   Inequality (2.6) is the Lyapunov estimate behind the whole convergence analysis; (2.7) gives $Cx_B^k \to CJ_{\gamma B}(z^*)$ strongly, Part 1(a) of Theorem 2.1.
--
--   **Formalization Note** As printed, (2.7) divides by $\gamma\lambda_k(2\beta - \gamma/\varepsilon)$ although the summands carry $\lambda_i$, $i \ge k$; it holds with $\lambda_k$ replaced by a uniform lower bound $\underline\lambda$ of the $\lambda_j$ (for instance $\inf_j \lambda_j$), which is how the proof uses it, and that version is stated. Summability of the series is part of the conclusion. The hypothesis $\sum_i \tau_i = \infty$ of Theorem 2.1 is not needed for these two inequalities and is omitted.
-- source:
--   Davis and Yin, A Three-Operator Splitting Scheme and its Optimization Applications, Set-Valued Var. Anal. 25 (2017), https://doi.org/10.1007/s11228-017-0421-z, p. 836, Eqs. (2.6) and (2.7) in the proof of Theorem 2.1

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ThreeOpSplitting_Convergence_MonotoneOperators
import Definitions.Def_ThreeOpSplitting_Convergence_ThreeOperatorIteration

namespace ThreeOpSplitting.Convergence

/-- Davis–Yin, Eqs. (2.6)–(2.7) (p. 836), from the proof of Theorem 2.1: the per-step descent
inequality (2.6) for Algorithm 1 against any fixed point `z*` of `T`, and its summed form
(2.7), stated with a lower bound `c ≤ λ_i` in place of the printed `λ_k`. -/
theorem descent_inequality {H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℝ H]
    [CompleteSpace H]
    (A B : H → Set H) (C : H → H) (β γ ε : ℝ) (JA JB : H → H) (lam : ℕ → ℝ) (z0 : H)
    (hA : IsMaximalMonotone A) (hB : IsMaximalMonotone B)
    (hβ : 0 < β) (hC : IsCocoercive β C)
    (hJA : IsResolvent γ A JA) (hJB : IsResolvent γ B JB)
    (hε0 : 0 < ε) (hε1 : ε < 1) (hγ0 : 0 < γ) (hγ : γ < 2 * β * ε)
    (hlam : ∀ j, 0 < lam j ∧ lam j < 1 / alpha ε)
    (zs : H) (hzs : zs ∈ Function.fixedPoints (threeOp γ JA JB C)) :
    let T := threeOp γ JA JB C
    let z := zSeq γ JA JB C lam z0
    let xB := xBSeq γ JA JB C lam z0
    (∀ k : ℕ,
        ‖z (k + 1) - zs‖ ^ 2 + tau ε (lam k) * ‖T (z k) - z k‖ ^ 2
          + γ * lam k * (2 * β - γ / ε) * ‖C (xB k) - C (JB zs)‖ ^ 2 ≤ ‖z k - zs‖ ^ 2) ∧
      ∀ c : ℝ, 0 < c → (∀ j, c ≤ lam j) → ∀ k : ℕ,
        Summable (fun i : ℕ => ‖C (xB (k + i)) - C (JB zs)‖ ^ 2) ∧
          ∑' i : ℕ, ‖C (xB (k + i)) - C (JB zs)‖ ^ 2
            ≤ ‖z k - zs‖ ^ 2 / (γ * c * (2 * β - γ / ε)) := by sorry

end ThreeOpSplitting.Convergence
